    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate leaning heavily on **Corbin Carroll**, who commands the day's peak score of 82.21. Facing R. V\u00e1squez, **Corbin Carroll** benefits from an elite 4.80 xERA matchup and a favorable platoon advantage that maximizes his speed-to-stolen-base potential. Alongside him, **Isaac Paredes** (67.49) serves as a secondary cornerstone; the combination of a +10% park factor and a +9% dynamic platoon boost makes him our most efficient bet for run production today. We are also monitoring **Brice Turang** (64.81), whose value is buoyed by a rare opportunity to exploit a slow pitcher delivery, providing a distinct path to a stolen base that remains our highest priority in this 5x5 Roto environment.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Vinnie Pasquantino** (42.87) on the bench. While his talent is clear, he faced a harsh convergence of negative factors: a tough 3.47 xERA opponent in Messick and a significant -15% hit to his projection due to the lefty-lefty platoon disadvantage. Consequently, **Cole Young** edged him out for the UTIL slot, despite a lower base, due to a more favorable matchup against Kikuchi. We remain cautious regarding **Jose Caballero**, whose inclusion in the lineup is currently based on an assumed #9 spot in the order; if he hits lower or is shifted, his current 50.85 score could diminish. Meanwhile, the core of **James Wood** (63.47) and **Griffin Conine** (61.48) are locked in as strong starts, anchored by their leadoff roles and positive SP skill matchups. We continue to hold **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, and **Mickey Moniak** on the bench due to injuries or lack of active status, while keeping an eye on long-term depth pieces like **Seiya Suzuki**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Max Muncy**, **Dalton Rushing**, and **Edwin Arroyo** should today's volatility necessitate a roster shuffle.",
